  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a fifteen-song set at The Salt Shed in Chicago on July 1, 2023 [1]. The lineup included tracks from albums such as The Sunset Tree, Tallahassee, and Bleed Out, alongside the unreleased song “You Were Cool” [1]. The band also played “Andrew Eldritch Is Moving Back to Leeds” and “Rain in Soho” from Goths, as well as “Palmcorder Yajna” from We Shall All Be Healed [1]. The set concluded with “Spent Gladiator 2” from Transcendental Youth [1]. The uploader noted that the drummer, Healy, was positioned centrally with a balanced distance, resulting in a clear and manageable audio capture [1]. This recording is the only one available for the date and is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones [1]. It is the 374th show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous performance at the same venue on June 30, 2023 [2]. An unnamed writer for Dying Scene documented the second night of the show at The Salt Shed [3]. The event was part of the venue’s 2023 indoor concert lineup [4].",
